{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["After He said, 'of the tree of knowledge you shall not eat,' what need is there for the word ממנו? Rather, He added it for clarification; likewise, 'she opened it and saw him, the child' (Exodus 2:6). Or its meaning is: even a little of it. The grammatical analysis of ממנו you will find in the Book of the Foundation. Know that the human was full of knowledge, for HaShem would not command one who has no knowledge. Only knowledge of good and evil regarding one matter alone he did not know. Do you not see that he called names to every beast and bird according to the nature of each one? Now he was a great sage, and had he not been so, HaShem would not have brought the creatures to him to see what he would call them — and He knows from him that he is a brute. Also HaShem showed him the tree of knowledge, for indeed his wife knew that it was in the midst of the garden."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והוא יודע ממנו שהוא בער' is rendered hyper-literally; the referent of 'he/He' and 'him' in this clause is textually ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:52.843210410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}